wxTRANSLATE( "Y = A OR B (after comparing each input with threshold)." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = A OR B (after comparing each input with threshold). No VCC/GND pins: all signal voltages use circuit ground as their reference. Output energy is provided by an ideal behavioral source; supply current and power limits are not modeled." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = A XNOR B after comparing both inputs with Input threshold. Output energy is ideal and supply current is not modeled. No supply pins are required. Signal and control voltages use circuit ground as reference." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = A XOR B after comparing both inputs with Input threshold. Output energy is ideal and supply current is not modeled. No supply pins are required. Signal and control voltages use circuit ground as reference." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when A != B (tolerance); otherwise LOW. Equality uses the absolute voltage difference and the configured tolerance. Output energy is ideal and supply current is not modeled. No supply pins are required. Signal and control voltages use circuit ground as reference." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when A < B; otherwise LOW. Output energy is ideal and supply current is not modeled. No supply pins are required. Signal and control voltages use circuit ground as reference." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when A < threshold; otherwise LOW." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when A < threshold; otherwise LOW. No VCC/GND pins: all signal voltages use circuit ground as their reference. Output energy is provided by an ideal behavioral source; supply current and power limits are not modeled." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when A <= B; otherwise LOW. Output energy is ideal and supply current is not modeled. No supply pins are required. Signal and control voltages use circuit ground as reference." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when A = B (tolerance); otherwise LOW. Equality uses the absolute voltage difference and the configured tolerance. Output energy is ideal and supply current is not modeled. No supply pins are required. Signal and control voltages use circuit ground as reference." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when A >= B; otherwise LOW. Output energy is ideal and supply current is not modeled. No supply pins are required. Signal and control voltages use circuit ground as reference." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when A >= threshold; otherwise LOW." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when A >= threshold; otherwise LOW. No VCC/GND pins: all signal voltages use circuit ground as their reference. Output energy is provided by an ideal behavioral source; supply current and power limits are not modeled." );
wxTRANSLATE( "Y = HIGH when Minimum <= V(Plus,Minus) <= Maximum; otherwise LOW. Plus and Minus are differential measurement inputs, not supply pins. Input loading is 1 teraohm between Plus and Minus. An inverted range always produces LOW. This tests voltage, not whether a wire is physically connected. Output energy is ideal and supply current is not modeled. No supply pins are required. Signal and control voltages use circuit ground as reference." );
